foundation.question_text:
A continuous random variable has $f(x) = \dfrac{3x^{2}}{56}$ on $[2,4]$, and $0$ elsewhere. Find the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.0cm, y=2.4cm]
\draw[->] (-0.6,0) -- (5.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.2) -- (0,1.25) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.5,0) -- (2,0);
\draw[thick, domain=2:4, smooth, samples=100, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.05357*\x*\x});
\draw (2,0) -- (2,0.2143);
\draw (4,0) -- (4,0.8571);
\draw[thick] (4,0) -- (5.2,0);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[below] at (4,0) {$4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A continuous random variable has cumulative distribution function $F(x) = \dfrac{x^{2} - 1}{24}$ on $[1,5]$. Find $P(X \ge 4)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.85cm, y=2.4cm]
\draw[->] (-0.6,0) -- (6.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.2) -- (0,1.45) node[above] {$F(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.5,0) -- (1,0);
\draw[thick, domain=1:5, smooth, samples=100, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{(\x*\x-1)/24});
\draw[thick] (5,1) -- (6.4,1);
\draw[dashed] (0,1) -- (5,1);
\node[left] at (0,1) {$1$};
\node[below] at (1,0) {$1$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A continuous random variable has $f(x) = \dfrac{1}{8}$ for $0 \le x < 4$ and $f(x) = \dfrac{1}{4}$ for $4 \le x \le 6$, and $0$ elsewhere. Find the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ on each piece.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.72cm, y=8cm]
\draw[->] (-0.8,0) -- (7.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.06) -- (0,0.34) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.7,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick] (0,0.125) -- (4,0.125);
\draw[thick] (4,0.25) -- (6,0.25);
\draw[dashed] (0,0.125) -- (0,0);
\draw[dashed] (4,0.125) -- (4,0.25);
\draw[dashed] (6,0.25) -- (6,0);
\draw[thick] (6,0) -- (7.4,0);
\node[left] at (0,0.125) {$\frac{1}{8}$};
\node[left] at (0,0.25) {$\frac{1}{4}$};
\node[below] at (4,0) {$4$};
\node[below] at (6,0) {$6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
A continuous random variable has $f(x) = \dfrac{4 + x}{16}$ for $-4 \le x \le 0$ and $f(x) = \dfrac{4 - x}{16}$ for $0 < x \le 4$, and $0$ elsewhere. Find the cumulative distribution function on each piece.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.55cm, y=8cm]
\draw[->] (-5.6,0) -- (5.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.06) -- (0,0.34) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-5.4,0) -- (-4,0);
\draw[thick] (-4,0) -- (0,0.25) -- (4,0);
\draw[thick] (4,0) -- (5.4,0);
\node[below left] at (-4,0) {$-4$};
\node[below right] at (4,0) {$4$};
\node[left] at (0,0.25) {$\frac{1}{4}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
